Okay, about the log message at the end of setupexport. Current end:

```c
	msg(LOG_INFO, "Size of exported file/device is %llu", (unsigned long long)client->exportsize);
	if(multifile) {
		msg(LOG_INFO, "Total number of files: %d", i);
	}
	return true;
```

Upstream has been added:

```c
	if(treefile) {
		msg(LOG_INFO, "Total number of (potential) files: %" PRId64, (client->exportsize+TREEPAGESIZE-1)/TREEPAGESIZE);
	}
```

client->exportsize is uint64_t, PRId64 expects int64_t → risk of format warning. The msg macro maps to syslog (ISSERVER undefined here? ISSERVER is undefined in config.h, so msg → g_log). To avoid format warnings while preserving meaning, we can use the same style as the line above, i.e. %llu + (unsigned long long). This also fits this file's convention better. I'll go with that.
Now the log message at the end of `setupexport`:

